                PrO-DmScHeCk was written in 100% assembler.


                     What is PrO-DmScHeCk ?
                     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
PrO-DmScHeCk is a DMS file checker meant to be run from a BBS when a
DMS file has been uploaded.

It allows other BBS adverts to be stripped from the file, and your own
BBS adverts can be added to advertise your BBS.

PrO-DmScHeCk was written in 680x0 assembler using Devpac 3 from HiSoft.

PrO-DmScHeCk needs kickstart 2.0 or better installed on your Amiga in
order for it to run, if there is enough need (ie at least 10 people
wanting it) then I'll do a 1.3 compatible version.


               PrO-DmScHeCk's command line options
               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Usage : PrO-DmScHeCk [<options>] <filename>

Where options is one or more of :

   BACK - Add a tail banner (from S:PDC_Banner_Rear)

   FRONT - Add a front banner (from S:PDC_Banner_Front)

   TRACK - Add a track 0 banner (from S:PDC_Track_Zero
                             this file MUST be 960 bytes long.)

Option in the REGISTERED version ONLY

   DATE - Add the current time and/or date to one/all of the
                text to be added.

      When '##-###-###' appears in a file the date will be added,
       and when '##:##' appears the current time will be added.


                    Installation instructions
                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Installation for normal command line usage

Copy PrO-DmScHeCk to anywhere in your path (usually C:).

Installation for Ami-Express BBS usage

Load Workbench and double click on the 'Install_PLC icon, or
open a shell and type 'execute Install_PLC'

Edit the files S:PDC_Banner_Front (any size),
               S:PDC_Banner_Rear (any size)
           and S:PDC_Track_Zero (960 bytes)

 to suit your own BBS.

Now when a DMS file is uploaded it will be automatically checked for
validity and integrity by PrO-DmScHeCk.


